      "data": {
        "view": {
          "intent": "node",
          "payload": "node.web.detail"
        },
        "semanticLevel": "detail",
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# What Does Twilite's Address Resolver Need?\n\nOne pure function over a small table of schemes and aliases. It returns the canonical address, how to fetch it, what kind of thing it is and whether it can be written. `gh://` and `yt://` are spellings; `web://` is \"a web resource\" and never replaces `http(s)://`."
        },
        "interfaceContract": {
          "version": 1,
          "ownsContent": true,
          "surfaceDelegation": true
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "0953fa34-568e-4500-88ed-dc18c9dede85"
        }
      }
    },
