      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# What Does Twilite's Address Resolver Need?\n\nTwilite understands `github://`, `tlz://`, `local://`, `https://` and root-relative addresses, each in its own corner of the code. This graph asks what one resolver would have to do, including the proposed `gh://`, `yt://` and `web://` forms.\n\n12 questions: 3 answered from the code, 9 open decisions with a recommendation for you to accept or change."
        },
        "renderShape": {
          "kind": "markdown"
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "0953fa34-568e-4500-88ed-dc18c9dede85"
        }
      },
      "handles": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "portId": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "input",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 180
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "address-resolver-notes",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "How This Was Written",
      "position": {
        "x": 300,
        "y": -1440
      },
      "width": 520,
      "height": 320,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 180
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# How this was written\n\nFrom reading the Twilite source on 2026-09-25 and a design discussion that proposed `gh://`, `yt://` and `web://`. File and line references were current when read. Nothing here is built or tested in a browser. Open questions carry a recommendation, not a decision."
        },
        "renderShape": {
          "kind": "markdown"
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "0953fa34-568e-4500-88ed-dc18c9dede85"
