      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "title": "One Resolver for Twilite Addresses",
        "description": "Twilite understands `github://`, `tlz://`, `local://`, `https://` and root-relative paths, each in its own corner of the code. This graph asks what a single resolver layer would have to do, including the proposed `gh://`, `yt://`, `youtube://` and `web://` forms, and separates what the code already does from what is only proposed.",
        "scope": "Addresses inside Twilite: links in Markdown and HTML views, Portal targets, the address bar, pasted text, class, Bridge and script refs, asset refs, and Save. Not in scope: registering schemes with the operating system or browser, or what a gh:// link does when it is pasted outside Twilite.",
        "notes": "Written 2026-09-25 from reading the Twilite source and a design discussion that proposed the aliases and web://. Nothing here is built or browser-tested. Answers to open questions are recommendations, not decisions.",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "0953fa34-568e-4500-88ed-dc18c9dede85"
        },
        "definitionKey": "qa-topic",
