      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "title": "Pieces of a resolver exist, but every caller parses for itself",
        "answer": "Four small pieces already do part of the job. `classifyTwiliteLink` (ten lines, in `twiliteLinks.js`) sorts a link into github, tlz, http-resource, blocked or external. `resourceAuthority` in `resourceResolution.js` names an address's authority (github, twilite, http or local). `graphRefLoader.js` normalizes a ref, builds a cache key and loads it. `Browser.js` turns `tlz://` into a fetchable URL.\n\nNothing ties them together. Twelve files test the raw `github://` prefix with `startsWith`, and about twenty-two contain a raw prefix test or regex of some kind: the Toolbar's Save logic, `GraphCrud.js`, `GraphEditor.js`, `GraphEditorContent.js`, `PortNode.js`, `scriptRefLoader.js`, `fragmentExtraction.js`, `lib/contentPaths.js` and others. Adding a scheme today means finding all of them, and they already differ: `parseGithubRef` treats an empty or trailing-slash path as `root.node`, while `parseGithubContentRef` returns null for an empty path.",
        "confidence": "high",
        "summary": "Partial resolvers exist in four places; about twenty-two files parse github:// themselves, and they already disagree.",
        "notes": "",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "0953fa34-568e-4500-88ed-dc18c9dede85"
        },
