      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "title": "Recommendation: yes. Aliases normalize once, at the edge",
        "answer": "Keep one canonical name per provider (`github`, `youtube`) and a small alias table (`gh` becomes `github`, `yt` becomes `youtube`). The resolver rewrites an alias to its canonical scheme before anything else runs, so nothing past the resolver ever sees `gh://`. The provider owns the meaning; an alias is only a spelling.\n\nNothing about this is invalid syntax: URI schemes are extensible. Scheme matching is already case-insensitive in `classifyTwiliteLink`, and the table should be too.\n\nThe rule for adding a scheme: a specialized scheme earns its place only when Twilite can do something more meaningful with it than open a web page. Otherwise use `web://`.",
        "confidence": "medium",
        "summary": "Two aliases, one canonical name each, rewritten before anything else runs.",
        "notes": "",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "0953fa34-568e-4500-88ed-dc18c9dede85"
        },
        "definitionKey": "qa-answer",
