      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "title": "Recommendation: `web://` means \"a web resource\"; `http(s)://` stay exact",
        "answer": "`web://host/path` means a generic web resource and resolves to `https://host/path`, the preferred transport. `https://` means exactly that, and `http://` means exactly that too; `web://` never downgrades to it. Neither is rejected or rewritten.\n\nThis changes little for navigation. An http(s) link is already \"http-resource\" in `classifyTwiliteLink`, is opened inside Twilite rather than in a new tab (`TlzLink`), and enters `fetchUrl` like any other address, where `resourceMediaKind` decides how the page is represented: html, markdown, pdf, image, text or a graph. `web://` would join that same path after its one rewrite.",
        "confidence": "medium",
        "summary": "web:// is one rewrite to https; http and https keep their exact meaning and the existing path.",
        "notes": "",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "0953fa34-568e-4500-88ed-dc18c9dede85"
        },
