      "data": {
        "title": "Following web://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cat",
        "example": "Someone writes `[cats](web://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cat)` in a Markdown node. The resolver reports scheme `web`, canonical `web://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cat` and transport `https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cat`. A click sends the transport address through the same `fetchUrl` path an ordinary https link uses today, and the page opens as a resource. A link written `http://oldmachine.local/x` in the same place keeps its scheme.",
        "relevance": "Shows that web:// adds one rewrite and nothing else.",
        "notes": "",
