      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "title": "Recommendation: a plain description, with no fetching inside it",
        "answer": "One pure function, `resolveAddress(input)`, returns a description and does no I/O:\n\n- `canonical`: aliases resolved and provider rules applied, such as `github://owner/repo/path`\n- `scheme` and `provider`\n- `kind`: graph, page, media, external or blocked\n- `transport`: the URL that can actually be fetched or embedded\n- `writable`: whether Twilite can save back to it\n- a display `label`\n- `diagnostics`: a code and a message for a malformed address, such as `gh://owner` with no repository\n\nLoaders take the description and do the fetching. `describeResource` in `resourceResolution.js` already returns a similar record (address, resolvedAddress, authority, mediaType, representation, status, reason), so this extends something that exists. An unknown scheme is not an error: it resolves to kind external and opens as it does today.",
        "confidence": "medium",
        "summary": "One pure function returning canonical, scheme, kind, transport, writable, label and diagnostics.",
        "notes": "",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "0953fa34-568e-4500-88ed-dc18c9dede85"
        },
        "definitionKey": "qa-answer",
