      "data": {
        "title": "Resolving gh://mikemartinez1974/public/primitives/root.node",
        "example": "Input `gh://mikemartinez1974/public/primitives/root.node`. Result: scheme `gh`, canonical `github://mikemartinez1974/public/primitives/root.node`, provider `github`, kind `graph`, transport the repository read the loader already makes (`/api/github/read`), writable `true` in principle. A Portal, the address bar and a Markdown link all receive this same answer, so a graph that stores the canonical form and a person who typed the alias end up in the same place.",
