      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "title": "Every place that takes an address, and one of them cannot yet",
        "answer": "- Markdown links: `TlzLink`, and the sanitizer in `MarkdownRenderer`, `MarkdownNode` and `MarkdownSurface`\n- Portal targets: `graphNavigationAddress.js`, `PortNode.js`\n- The address bar and Open box: `Browser.js`, `setAddress`\n- The `?doc=` launch parameter: `BrowserExperience.js`, `buildTwiliteLaunchUrl`\n- Pasted text: `pasteHandler.js`\n- Class, Bridge and script refs: `nodeClassContract.js`, `scriptRefLoader.js`, the edge class registry\n- Asset refs for images and video: `PropertiesPanel.js`, `contentPaths.js`\n- Save and Save As: `Toolbar.js`, `DocumentPropertiesDialog.js`\n\nOne cannot be routed at all today. HTML views render in a sandboxed iframe (`DynamicViewNode.js`), and the only click bridge I found there handles `data-twilite-control`. An `<a href=\"gh://…\">` in a class view therefore goes nowhere. Agents and the onboarding docs (`AGENTS.md`, `OnboardLLM.md`) describe address forms in prose and would need the same table.",
        "confidence": "medium",
        "summary": "Eight surfaces take addresses; links inside HTML views are not routed at all today.",
        "notes": "",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "0953fa34-568e-4500-88ed-dc18c9dede85"
        },
        "definitionKey": "qa-answer",
