      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "title": "It has to be generated from the table, because it is copied by hand today",
        "answer": "The Markdown sanitizer removes the link target from any scheme not on its allowlist. `TWILITE_INTERNAL_LINK_PROTOCOLS` (`['tlz', 'github']`) is added to it in `MarkdownRenderer.js`, `MarkdownNode.js` and `MarkdownSurface.js`. `DynamicViewNode.js` (line 5585 when I read it) repeats the list by hand instead of importing the constant.\n\nSo a `gh://`, `yt://` or `web://` link written in Markdown would lose its target however good the resolver is. The allowlist must be derived from the resolver's scheme table, canonical names and aliases both, and the hand-written copy removed.",
        "confidence": "high",
        "summary": "The allowlist is hand-copied in four places; derive it from the scheme table or new schemes lose their links.",
        "notes": "",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "0953fa34-568e-4500-88ed-dc18c9dede85"
        },
        "definitionKey": "qa-answer",
