      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "title": "Recommendation: write canonical, accept anything, keep the typed form only as a label",
        "answer": "Store the canonical form in everything Twilite writes: Portal `target.ref`, Bridge and class refs, `document.url`, edge endpoints. Accept aliases when reading and when typed.\n\nReasons: cache keys and duplicate detection compare refs, and `normalizeGraphRefCacheKey` already lowercases owner and repository for GitHub, which is exactly the kind of rule the resolver should own. Validation messages such as the one in `nodeClassContract.js` (\"classRef must be a valid ref (github://, local://, tlz://, /, http(s)://)\") would otherwise need every alias added by hand. And a graph that says `gh://` in some places and `github://` in others is two spellings of one thing.\n\nThe cost is that a person's chosen spelling is lost on save. Keep it as the link label if it matters.",
        "confidence": "medium",
        "summary": "Canonical form on write, any form on read; the typed spelling survives only as a label.",
        "notes": "",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "0953fa34-568e-4500-88ed-dc18c9dede85"
        },
        "definitionKey": "qa-answer",
