      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "title": "Recommendation: block by scheme, and never let graph data define a scheme",
        "answer": "Keep what `classifyTwiliteLink` does now: `javascript:`, `data:` and `file:` links are blocked and drawn as plain text, and external links open in a new tab with `noopener noreferrer`. Add three rules.\n\n1. The scheme and alias table is code, not graph data. A shared graph must not be able to declare that `gh://` means something else.\n2. `web://` resolves only to https, never http.\n3. A provider that embeds (YouTube) may embed only from a fixed list of origins, in a sandboxed frame.\n\n\"Blocked\" depends on how the address is used, not on the scheme alone. See the caveat.",
        "confidence": "medium",
        "summary": "Keep the current blocked schemes; the table is code; web:// is https only; embeds are sandboxed and origin-limited.",
        "notes": "",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "0953fa34-568e-4500-88ed-dc18c9dede85"
        },
        "definitionKey": "qa-answer",
        "_classBinding": {
