      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "title": "Recommendation: resolve and open it now; decide the representation later",
        "answer": "`youtube://ID` (and `yt://ID`) canonicalizes to a video id. For navigation it resolves to `https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ID`, for embedding to the `youtube-nocookie.com` embed URL, and it can carry an optional `t=` start time.\n\nWhat Twilite should make of it is not settled by the code. `resourceMediaKind` has no video kind (it knows graph, html, markdown, text, image and pdf), Content has no video kind, and video is handled today as an asset ref (`PropertiesPanel.js`, `pasteHandler.js`). The choice is a new Content kind, a dedicated embed node, or a View that embeds it.\n\nRecommend shipping `youtube` as a provider that resolves and opens correctly, and choosing the representation when a graph actually needs one.",
        "confidence": "low",
        "summary": "Resolve and open now; pick a video representation only when a real graph needs one.",
        "notes": "",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "0953fa34-568e-4500-88ed-dc18c9dede85"
        },
