      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "title": "Recommendation: `writable` is part of the description",
        "answer": "Today Save decides for itself. `Toolbar.js` parses `github://` in three places to find the repository and path, handles `local://` through a file handle, and `DocumentPropertiesDialog.js` builds the address back from repository and path.\n\n`github://` is the address written through Twilite's GitHub integration, and `local://` is written through a file handle. `web`, `http(s)` and `youtube` are read-only, and so, as far as I found, is `tlz`. Put `writable` (and the mechanism) in the description so Save asks the resolver instead of parsing.\n\nWhether the signed-in person may actually write is a permission question the address cannot answer. The resolver should say \"can be written in principle\" and leave the check to the GitHub layer.",
        "confidence": "medium",
        "summary": "writable lives in the description; permission stays with the GitHub layer.",
        "notes": "",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "0953fa34-568e-4500-88ed-dc18c9dede85"
        },
