      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "title": "Recommendation: yes, but only the part links depend on",
        "answer": "The design discussion recommended doing this before the Page Template, and I agree for one reason: a page is mostly links, and the template would otherwise encode today's link behavior. Bound it.\n\n1. One module and a scheme table (github/gh, youtube/yt, web, http, https, tlz, local, root-relative), the description above, and tests.\n2. Move the Markdown allowlist, `classifyTwiliteLink`, `TlzLink` and the address bar onto it, and route HTML-view links through the same call.\n3. Ongoing: migrate the remaining raw-prefix sites one file at a time, guarded by a test that counts `startsWith('github://')` outside the resolver and only lets the number fall (twelve files today).\n\nSteps 1 and 2 are what the Page Template needs. Step 3 does not block it.",
        "confidence": "medium",
        "summary": "Do steps 1 and 2 first; the migration of the other files is a ratchet that does not block the template.",
        "notes": "",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "0953fa34-568e-4500-88ed-dc18c9dede85"
        },
